AIRTP — AIRTP Intelligent Realtime Transport Protocol

Copyright (c) 2026 Trey

This repository contains the reference implementation of AIRTP (AIRTP Intelligent Realtime Transport Protocol), an open-source experimental protocol for transport-independent AI communication.

AIRTP explores a layered architecture that separates AI model interfaces from the underlying transport, enabling applications to communicate with AI services through a consistent protocol abstraction. The project investigates concepts including transport abstraction, capability negotiation, session lifecycle management, structured message envelopes, chunk metadata and reassembly, and provider-agnostic model interfaces.

The software is intended as a research and educational reference implementation demonstrating how AI communication can be treated as a protocol engineering problem rather than a provider-specific API integration. The architecture is designed to isolate application logic from transport implementation details while supporting interchangeable AI backends through a common session interface.

